The patch introduces a concrete security weakness in SPA fallback file serving and a portability bug in the new dynamic symbol resolver, and also has an API-routing edge case that can mis-handle namespace-root paths. These defects are actionable and should be fixed before accepting the change.

Full review comments:

- [P1] Guard SPA fallback paths before file read — /home/wali/Desktop/AI BOT REBUILD/v2/backend/app/main.py:207-207
  The catch-all handler builds `public_dir / full_path` directly from the URL segment and serves it with `FileResponse` when it is a file. A crafted request path containing `..` segments can escape the `v2/frontend/public` tree and read files outside the intended static directories whenever `dist/` exists, turning an SPA fallback into an unintended local-file read path.

- [P2] Resolve symbol-runtime repository root dynamically — /home/wali/Desktop/AI BOT REBUILD/v2/backend/app/services/v2_symbol_runtime_universe.py:31-34
  The new symbol resolver hardcodes `REPO` to `/home/wali/Desktop/AI BOT REBUILD`, so any checkout/agent running this module from a different path will fail to load the published symbol-universe payload and silently fall back to baseline symbols. That defeats the dynamic-universe behavior this change is meant to enforce and makes the new resolver non-portable across environments.

- [P3] Handle bare namespace roots in SPA route filter — /home/wali/Desktop/AI BOT REBUILD/v2/backend/app/main.py:193-194
  The namespace filter uses only `startswith("api/")` and `startswith("public/")`, so requests to `/api` or `/public` fall through to the SPA catch-all and return HTML instead of a 404. This can hide missing-route conditions for clients or probes that legitimately query the namespace roots directly.
